#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/parameterization/parameterization.ipynb:272
msgid "Adding the parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/parameterization/parameterization.ipynb:274
msgid ""
"Now we can proceed to the step where we add the ``parameter`` values using a "
"dictionary. We set up a dictionary with parameter names as the dictionary "
"keys and their respective values as the dictionary values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/parameterization/parameterization.ipynb:-1
msgid "[6]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/parameterization/parameterization.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"def D_fun(c):\n"
"    return 3.9  # * pybamm.exp(-c)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"values = {\n"
"    \"Particle radius [m]\": 2,\n"
"    \"Diffusion coefficient [m2.s-1]\": D_fun,\n"
"    \"Initial concentration [mol.m-3]\": 2.5,\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/parameterization/parameterization.ipynb:303
msgid ""
"Now we can pass this dictionary in ``pybamm.ParameterValues`` class which "
"accepts a dictionary of parameter names and values. We can then print "
"``param`` to check if it was initialised."
